2. Common UML Symbols
Symbol	Meaning
Rectangle	Class or Interface
Arrow with hollow triangle	Inheritance / Implementation
Line	Association
Diamond	Aggregation (hollow) / Composition (filled)
+ / - / #	Public / Private / Protected
3. Frequently Used Design Patterns
Pattern	Use Case	Example
Singleton	One instance needed globally	Logger, Configuration Manager
Factory	Create objects without exposing instantiation	VehicleFactory creates Car/Bus
Builder	Construct complex objects step by step	Building a House object with rooms, doors
Observer	Notify multiple objects on state change	Notification Service, Event System
Strategy	Switch algorithm dynamically	Payment method selection
Decorator	Add functionality dynamically	Adding filters to streams or API responses
